# AI-Assisted: Claude Code (model: claude-sonnet-5) - .gitignore for the curated rules-data
# pipeline repository (T003). The work/ rule is the first and most important line: raw acquired
# source material must never be committed to any repository (FR-010).

# Ephemeral raw source -- NEVER committed. Emptied at the start and end of every run.
work/

# Local operator configuration. It is where WGC_MECHANIC_DIGEST_KEY sits on a curator's machine,
# and an untracked-but-not-ignored file is one `git add -A` away from being a committed secret.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
# Anchored to the repository root: an unanchored `build/` would also swallow the
# pipeline's own `pipeline/build/` stage package, which is source, not an artifact.
/dist/
/build/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# The disagreement set's build output and reports are test artifacts. `fixtures/minimal/build/`
# is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the published fixture bundle the consuming app's CI
# ingests, and it must stay in review (FR-048).
fixtures/disagreements/build/
# The minimal set's committed artifact is the bundle and the curated tree the consuming app
# ingests; its report is a by-product of regenerating them.
fixtures/minimal/build/reports/

# `reports/candidate/` is the local scratch-build destination -- a by-product regenerated on
# every operator run, not a reviewed artifact. Versioned run reports (`reports/<id>/`, e.g.
# `reports/mfm-2026-08/`) stay tracked; only the `candidate` slug is ignored.
reports/candidate/
